{
    "_comment": "Which raw file becomes which shipped sound (read by tools/process-audio.mjs; the set names and variant counts must equal SAMPLE_SETS in client/src/audio-logic.ts, a test checks it). 'match' are regular expressions tried in order against the file name without its extension; the first 'n' distinct files found become variants 1..n. 'cuts' ([file regex, start second, optional dB, optional length]) cut one variant each out of a long recording (package N: several gunshots or breaths in one file; start times were read off the waveform, 3 ms before the onset). 'prefer' is an alternative tried first when its files exist. 'maxDur' cuts the sound (s, 'fade' long fade-out, default 30 ms), 'pitch' is a playback-speed factor, 'hp'/'lp' filters in Hz, 'denoise' dB, 'fadeIn' s, 'gain' dB applied after peak normalisation. Package H's Kenney names were written before the packs were available and have since been checked.",
